1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 8th generation. Before 2000 BC to ? Son of Yun (云). Also known as Jia (嘉).
2 CONT
2 CONT A Marquis/Lord of Jiangxia (江夏侯) of Huang State (黄国), in the present Huguang Prefecture (湖广) in Wuchang (武昌).
2 CONT
2 CONT Had a son - Zu Zhong (祖仲).
2 CONT
2 CONT Took part in the fight against Xia (夏) control.
2 CONT
2 CONT 八世。约公元前2000 ---。云之子, 祖仲之父。封黄侯, 参加反抗夏朝斗争。
2 CONT
2 CONT NB - Between Xiong Qi (熊启) and the first ancestor, Xuan Yuan (轩辕), some internet sources list several ancestors that are based on folklore. They are therefore difficult to verify. For the purpose of my family tree, I had adopted t
2 CONC he record of our Family Genealogy Book, Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱) and Yanjingcun's Genealogy Book, Huang Shi Ying Zuo Fang Yuan Qu Wu Hao Zhi Pu (黄氏英佐房园趣无号支谱) for the preceding generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES (资料来源) -
2 CONT
