1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Chang Ruo''' - From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Chang Ruo''' (Chinese: 昌若; pinyin: Chāng Ruò;?–?)The ancestors of the Shang dynasty. His family name is '''Zi''' (子)。The fourth leader of the Shang tribe.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''History'''
2 CONT
2 CONT His great-grandfather was Xie. His grandfather was Zhao Ming. His father was Xiang Tu. His son was Cao Yu, the founding monarch of the Tang ancestors.
2 CONT
2 CONT In order to domesticate the horses, his father, Xiang Tu, was in the position of Xiang of Xia, and the horse was made.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Xiang Tu, Chang Ruo succeeded. When Chang Ruo died, his son, Cao Yu, succeeded;[1] but because the name of Chang Ruo appears later, it may be a fictitious one.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT *Great-great-grandfather: Emperor Ku (帝嚳)
2 CONT **Great-grandfather: Xie (契)
2 CONT ***Grandfather: Zhao Ming (昭明)
2 CONT ****Father: Xiang Tu (相土)
2 CONT *****Son: Cao Yu (曹圉)
