1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 26th generation. Approximately 1525 BC  to _____.  Son of Zu Jia (祖甲).
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Madam Jia (贾氏) who bore him a son - Lin (廪) - after a 215-day gestation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lived during the Shang (商) Dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT 二十六世。约公元前1525 ---。祖甲之子, 廪之父。娶贾氏, 孕二百十五日而生子廪。
2 CONT
2 CONT NB - Our Family Genealogy Book, Wen Ming Zu JIa Pu (文明祖家谱), recorded that Madam Jia gave birth to Lin after a 15 -month pregnancy. It was probably an error. The 215-day gestation is based on the account in 黄正瑞的博客. In it, Lin's mot
2 CONC her was written as Madam Cao (曹氏), probably the result of an error in interpreting the original Chinese character. For the purpose of my Family Tree, I have adopted the record of my Family Genealogy Book that Lin's mother was Mada
2 CONC m Jia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES (资料来源) -
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Wen Ming Zu Jia Pu (文明祖家谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Huang Shi Ying Zuo Fang Yuan Qu Wu Hao Zhi Pu (黄氏英佐房园趣无号支谱).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. 黄守恭 - 百度百科.
2 CONT
