2 CONT uke Yi of Qi (Chinese: 齊乙公; pinyin: Qí Yǐ Gōng), personal name Lü De, was the third recorded ruler of the Qi state.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Yi succeeded his father, Duke Ding, and was in turn succeeded by his son, Duke Gui.[1][2]
