1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marquis Cheng of Cai (蔡成侯) was a ruler of the State of Cai during ancient China. He was the son of Marquis Zhao of Cai (蔡昭侯) and N.N. of Cheng. He was also the father of N.N. of Tsai.
2 CONT
2 CONT The State of Cai was a regional power during the Zhou dynasty, often caught in conflicts with larger neighboring states. Marquis Cheng's lineage was part of the House of Ji, which was connected to the Royal House of Zhou.
