2 CONT Hsien Kung of Yan (燕獻公) was a ruler of the State of Yan (燕国) during ancient China. He was the son of Ping Kung of Yan (燕平公) and the father of Hsiao Kung of Yan (燕孝公). His reign took place during the Warring States period (475–221 
2 CONC BCE).
