1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''The 42nd Ancestor: 天榮 (Tiān Róng)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The 42nd Generation Ancestor, 天榮 (Tiān Róng), was born in 1123 BC. He was the 侍禦郎 (Shì Yù Láng) of the later Shang Dynasty. His wives were 岑 (Cén) and 魚 (Yú ).
2 CONT
2 CONT 岑 (Cén) gave birth to three sons named 瓊國 (Qióng Guó), 華正 (Huá Zhèng), 木仁 (Mù Rén). 魚 (Yú ) gave birth to three daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 妲己 (Dá Jǐ) killed both madams by using a cruel punishment named 炮烙 (Páo Lào) and we do not even know where they were buried.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Apparently,  瓊國 (Qióng Guó), was later referred to by combining Tan with 瓊 (Qióng) and Tan with 國 (Guó): Henry Tom)
