1 OCCU Hsiung-nu-King of China 173-162 BC, 5th King of the 1st XIONGNU Dynasty, Chanyu des Xiongnu
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kokkhan, 3rd King of the Huns, aka Laoshan; aka Chi-Yu; 5th King of the 1st XIONGNU Dynasty, died after 161 BC.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Laoshang Shanyu (r. 174–160 BC) was a Chanyu of the Xiongnu, the successor to Modu Shanyu. During his reign the expansion of Xiongnu power continued; the Yuezhi were defeated, and the Xiongnu thus gained control of the Hexi region
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laoshang_Shanyu
2 CONT
2 CONT 174 BC Kokkhan (Laoshan-Giyui-Shanyu (Aga-Yui Shanyu: Ch. “Laoshang“ = “old and elevated” =. Türkic “Aga”, “[A]Giyui“ = “Aga-Yui”, 174-161 BC) Huns (Hsiung-nu) attack Tocharians (Yüeh-chih, Yuezhi, White Huns), driving them from G
2 CONC ansu. In 160 AD on behalf of Huns the war was run by Usuns, supposedly in retribution for their displacement and genocide by Tochars in 410 BC. Usuns presented Laoshan Shanyu with head of Tochar leader, which was made into drinkin
2 CONC g cup and used for sacral ceremonies, including oath on heqin treaty with China 
